<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">History of the Great Island of Madagascar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1658">1658</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Histoire de la grande isle Madagascar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The History of the Great Island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> (Histoire de la grande isle Madagascar) is a book by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etienne-de-flacourt">Étienne de Flacourt</a>, French governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taolagnaro">Fort-Dauphin</a>, published in 1658. Drawing on his years in the colony from 1648, it describes the geography, plants, animals, peoples and customs of Madagascar, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanosy">Antanosy</a>. It was the most important European account of the island for over a century.</p></div>
